---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/about/"]}>
  <main id="main">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">About Otto by Tebra</span>
      </nav>
      <article class="content-narrow prose">
        <div class="eyebrow">Otto by Tebra</div>
        <h1>About Otto by Tebra</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Otto by Tebra is an AI-native EHR for mental health providers.
        </p>
        <p>
          The public product brings together AI-drafted notes, clinician review,
          scheduling, telehealth, patient records, and payments. This resource
          site helps independent practices work through the business questions
          around that care.
        </p>
        <h2>Practical support between sessions.</h2>
        <p>
          The journal covers session rates, superbills, and Good Faith
          Estimates. Companion tools show their assumptions and let you prepare
          a document or calculation using your own inputs.
        </p>
        <p>
          Articles link to their sources and include a date. We avoid
          unsupported outcome claims and identify where a calculation or
          workflow needs a practice-specific decision.
        </p>
        <div class="tool-support">
          <a href="/mental-health-ehr/">Explore the product ↗</a>
          <a href="/blog/">Read the journal ↗</a>
          <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial approach ↗</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
